Timeline
- 3dup is not in gforth 0.7.3; defined locally in solve.fs.
- macOS make is GNU 3.81, which ignores .RECIPEPREFIX: use gmake.
- BSD sed has no \b; the register-flag rename went through perl.
- First baseline took 7 instructions on the worked example (optimum 4):
  it never checked whether two held values combine into a target. The
  reuse variant adds that check and finds 4.

Reproduction
  gmake -C experiments/011-elf-calculator test
  -> PASS baseline: 100 programs, 58030 instructions
  -> PASS reuse: 100 programs, 53229 instructions
  -> PASS 5 negative controls rejected (divide, limit, subtract, undefined, csv)
  cell: 8 bytes (gforth 0.7.3, darwin arm64)
